1
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:04,800
Have your injuries improved
any, Avdol? They have.

2
00:00:04,980 --> 00:00:06,380
As relieved as I am.

3
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:09,277
I'm even more relieved
knowing you're alright.

4
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:13,237
Yes, well, I'm fortunate there was
no significant damage to my cornea.

5
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:15,457
I'm expected to make a full recovery.

6
00:00:15,540 --> 00:00:17,437
This takes me back to middle school.

7
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:19,657
During what should have
been an ordinary game,

8
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:22,357
one of my classmates took
a baseball to the eye.

9
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:24,322
He was good as new the next day.

10
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:27,677
And as it turned out, his eye
had only lost a bit of fluid.

11
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:29,054
Wait, are you serious?

12
00:00:29,680 --> 00:00:30,510
No.

13
00:00:30,593 --> 00:00:34,965
I'll get these bandages off in no time,
and I'll catch up with you in a few days.

14
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:37,700
In 800 kilometers are Cairo and Dio.

15
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:41,220
Everyone, you must remain vigilant.

16
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:44,577
Now let's see.

17
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:48,057
What kind of language is this
hospital bill written in anyway?

18
00:00:48,140 --> 00:00:52,477
I guess it's supposed to be Arabic,
but man, if this crap isn't confusing.

19
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:56,337
The zero is a five, the decimal
is a zero, and the seven is a six.

20
00:00:56,420 --> 00:01:00,237
And what the heck is this wormy-looking
thingamajig supposed to be?

21
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:02,577
It's a four, so the amount we owe is...

22
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:05,480
46,350 Egyptian pounds!

23
00:01:05,580 --> 00:01:06,420
That's insane!

24
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:08,840
Oh, my God!

25
00:01:09,380 --> 00:01:10,900
What kind of dog is he?

26
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:11,830
He's so funny looking.

27
00:01:11,913 --> 00:01:12,743
Look at that.

28
00:01:12,826 --> 00:01:14,277
Why in the world is he chewing gum?

29
00:01:14,360 --> 00:01:16,184
He must be waiting for someone.

30
00:01:16,460 --> 00:01:17,931
Such a good little doggy.

31
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:20,937
And here I thought Iggy
was waiting for us outside.

32
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:21,850
Good grief.

33
00:01:21,933 --> 00:01:23,537
Looks like he's a hit with the ladies.

34
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:26,057
Should we tell him doggies
don't usually chew gum?

35
00:01:26,140 --> 00:01:28,000
What a peculiar little puppy.

36
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:29,257
Hello there, ladies.

37
00:01:29,340 --> 00:01:30,170
Hmm?

38
00:01:30,253 --> 00:01:32,477
Here's a little bit of
friendly advice for you girls.

39
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:34,417
Step away if you know what's good for you.

40
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:37,497
I know he comes across as a
charming furball at first,

41
00:01:37,580 --> 00:01:40,757
but deep in his soul, he harbors
an extreme hatred for people.

42
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:43,546
If you're not careful
when you least expect...

43
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:45,537
What the hell are you doing?!

44
00:01:45,620 --> 00:01:47,326
Get off of me, you damn mutt!

45
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:51,860
You're such a beauty!

46
00:01:52,340 --> 00:01:53,857
Oh, you get along so well!

47
00:01:53,940 --> 00:01:56,397
In your dreams, we don't get along at all.

48
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:57,310
Damn it, Iggy.

49
00:01:57,400 --> 00:01:58,757
Would you get the hell off of me?

50
00:01:58,840 --> 00:02:00,257
We'll catch you guys later.

51
00:02:00,340 --> 00:02:01,820
See you, lovebirds. Mr.

52
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:03,317
Joestar, please help me.

53
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:05,341
Hey, hang on a minute, would you?

54
00:02:07,060 --> 00:02:08,100
What the hell?

55
00:02:08,940 --> 00:02:11,200
You nasty little mutt!

56
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:41,360
I don't know.

57
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:22,020
The end of the world

58
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:44,760
In ancient times,

59
00:03:44,920 --> 00:03:46,697
Egyptians were in the
habit of burying their dead

60
00:03:46,780 --> 00:03:49,604
on the west bank of the
Nile where the sun sets.

61
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:53,857
That's the reason Egyptian cities
stand on the east side of the Nile.

62
00:03:53,940 --> 00:03:55,417
On the west side, however,

63
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:59,382
you're likely to find graves and
mortuary temples scattered about.

64
00:03:59,760 --> 00:04:02,466
But our enemies don't
care about east or west.

65
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:05,972
They'll come from whatever
direction is most advantageous.

66
00:04:10,300 --> 00:04:15,120
Look, I know you didn't ask for my opinion,
but your cows are far too lethargic.

67
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:17,927
Although they're strong,
I'll give them that.

68
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:19,360
Hey, Chaka!

69
00:04:19,580 --> 00:04:20,698
Move your ass, boy!

70
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:23,567
And would you stop
dragging the rear already?

71
00:04:25,460 --> 00:04:26,640
What a disgrace!

72
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:27,940
Some man you are!

73
00:04:28,180 --> 00:04:29,700
How are you, my son?

74
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:34,652
Looks like your son and your
cow have something in common.

75
00:04:41,420 --> 00:04:42,297
A sword?

76
00:04:42,380 --> 00:04:45,500
What's something like this
doing out here? Hey, look!

77
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:46,600
It's a sword!

78
00:04:47,780 --> 00:04:48,610
Give me that!

79
00:04:48,693 --> 00:04:49,523
Look at that!

80
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:50,597
Must have been dropped!

81
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:52,677
I can't believe no one's
come back to claim it!

82
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:56,617
Their loss is our gain, because this
sword is probably worth a fortune.

83
00:04:56,700 --> 00:04:59,229
Hey, what if the owner's
still in the area?

84
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:01,797
Poor guy must be
panicking right about now.

85
00:05:01,880 --> 00:05:04,797
On the off chance it's some
kind of fancy-schmancy artifact,

86
00:05:04,880 --> 00:05:06,117
shouldn't we give it to the police?

87
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:07,030
You idiot!

88
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:10,337
This sword could be the end
of all of our money troubles!

89
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:12,200
But I'm the one who found it.

90
00:05:12,460 --> 00:05:14,677
It won't be worth a damn
thing if it's blunt.

91
00:05:14,760 --> 00:05:16,237
Pull it out so we can take a look.

92
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:17,150
Right.

93
00:05:21,980 --> 00:05:22,810
What's wrong?

94
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:24,940
The damn thing won't budge!

95
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:26,877
Why the hell won't it come out?

96
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:27,940
That's weird.

97
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:29,560
Let me try it. Take it.

98
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:32,320
You hold this end. Right.

99
00:05:38,900 --> 00:05:40,260
It's no use!

100
00:05:40,460 --> 00:05:42,989
The blade hasn't moved
a single centimeter!

101
00:05:43,140 --> 00:05:44,611
Father, let me have a go.

102
00:05:45,100 --> 00:05:46,080
Oh, shut up!

103
00:05:46,260 --> 00:05:49,789
If I can't free it, what chance
does an idiot like you have?

104
00:05:50,880 --> 00:05:51,740
My hands!

105
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:53,471
What happened to my hand?

106
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:56,780
My hand!

107
00:05:57,060 --> 00:05:58,600
Why is it spewing blood?

108
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:02,277
How the hell did the sword cut me?

109
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:04,977
We pulled on a damn thing, but
the blade wouldn't come out!

110
00:06:05,060 --> 00:06:06,937
All I did was grab it by the hill!

111
00:06:07,020 --> 00:06:09,037
There's something
strange about that sword.

112
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:11,777
Hey, uh, you think now's
a good time for me to try?

113
00:06:11,860 --> 00:06:13,100
You know what? Fine.

114
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:15,182
Go ahead and try it if you want.

115
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:32,120
It came out so easy, I didn't put
the slightest bit of effort into it.

116
00:06:33,580 --> 00:06:34,410
What?

117
00:06:34,493 --> 00:06:35,340
I can hear it.

118
00:06:35,840 --> 00:06:37,160
This makes no sense.

119
00:06:37,620 --> 00:06:39,460
I can hear the blade ringing.

120
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:45,757
I'm by no means an expert when it comes
to swords or things of that nature,

121
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:48,757
but I don't think I've ever
encountered a blade this beautiful.

122
00:06:48,840 --> 00:06:50,637
It's like a rare Japanese katana.

123
00:06:50,720 --> 00:06:53,217
It glistens like it's
cloaked in ice-cold water.

124
00:06:53,300 --> 00:06:55,757
We've been graced with
an amazing discovery!

125
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:57,075
Hand it over, my boy!

126
00:06:57,320 --> 00:07:01,320
I don't like you, has no business
wielding such a valuable treasure!

127
00:07:04,980 --> 00:07:07,060
Oh god! Seiko! Why?

128
00:07:07,420 --> 00:07:10,300
Why would you do this thing out? Father!

129
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:12,737
I don't know what happens.

130
00:07:12,820 --> 00:07:15,337
You were standing behind me,
and before I knew it, the sword!

131
00:07:15,420 --> 00:07:17,060
It's not my fault, I swear!

132
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:18,837
Why are you just standing there?

133
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:22,567
We have to hurry and get him to
a doctor before it's too late!

134
00:07:27,500 --> 00:07:28,760
This sword is evil!

135
00:07:28,980 --> 00:07:32,156
It's almost as though the
blade has a mind of its own!

136
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:38,140
Be calm.

137
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:42,717
Still your heart, Chaka.

138
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:44,677
Their deaths mean nothing.

139
00:07:44,760 --> 00:07:46,720
Nothing whatsoever, Chaka.

140
00:07:48,020 --> 00:07:48,850
Just...

141
00:07:48,933 --> 00:07:49,940
just who are you?

142
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:53,440
I can't see you, but
I can hear your voice.

143
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:58,880
I am the stand of the god
Anubis, ruler of the underworld,

144
00:07:59,260 --> 00:08:02,020
deity of embalming, and lord of the dead.

145
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:04,520
You have unsheathed me.

146
00:08:04,960 --> 00:08:06,980
Thus you shall be my standard.

147
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:08,760
You are a virtuoso.

148
00:08:09,220 --> 00:08:10,637
So I shall make you master the world.

149
00:08:10,720 --> 00:08:12,677
No one of the soul is stronger than you.

150
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:15,400
You shall wield me and you shall kill.

151
00:08:19,980 --> 00:08:24,437
Father and that man deserve to die, so
they should be thrilled that I killed them.

152
00:08:24,520 --> 00:08:27,357
I think I'll hack you to
pieces while I'm on a roll.

153
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:28,477
Why you Minichaka?

154
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:29,857
You don't really want to do this.

155
00:08:29,940 --> 00:08:30,897
Please let me live, okay?

156
00:08:30,980 --> 00:08:32,740
Oh, I don't want to die!

157
00:08:37,660 --> 00:08:39,640
How the hell did he do that?

158
00:08:40,060 --> 00:08:42,580
Somehow the cow's completely unharmed!

159
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:53,220
Slaughter Joseph.

160
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:55,520
Slice Polnareff.

161
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:57,917
Cleave Jotaro in two.

162
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:02,440
No, you are a fighting
genius, a master of the sword.

163
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:05,546
No one in the world is
a match for your blade.

164
00:09:05,740 --> 00:09:06,680
No one!

165
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:11,140
Come on, Bo.

166
00:09:11,540 --> 00:09:15,017
Come on, do we really have time
to lounge around in this place?

167
00:09:15,100 --> 00:09:16,688
Would you quit complaining?

168
00:09:16,840 --> 00:09:19,517
They've been kind enough to
allow us passage on their ferry,

169
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:21,247
so we must show our respect.

170
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:25,697
I don't know about you guys, but I'm
starving, so let's get something to eat.

171
00:09:25,780 --> 00:09:27,427
Wow, you never stop, do you?

172
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:30,037
Here, this should tide you over for now.

173
00:09:30,120 --> 00:09:32,061
You know damn well that's Iggy's!

174
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:34,278
Would you just take the gum already?

175
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:37,120
Hey, where's the bathroom, huh?

176
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:38,555
Shall we look for it?

177
00:09:39,720 --> 00:09:41,400
Hey, mister, over here.

178
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:43,440
Wanna buy some papyrus?

179
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:45,779
This papyrus is the original paper.

180
00:09:46,020 --> 00:09:47,597
Want a piece of Egyptian history?

181
00:09:47,680 --> 00:09:48,557
Here, take a look.

182
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:51,960
This is 100 % Bone Feet
papyrus. Papyrus, huh?

183
00:09:52,180 --> 00:09:53,768
I'll give you a good price.

184
00:09:53,940 --> 00:09:56,057
Are you positive this is the real thing?

185
00:09:56,140 --> 00:09:57,157
Of course, my friend.

186
00:09:57,240 --> 00:10:01,317
And I'll have you know a famous Egyptian
craftsman drew this, so it's quite genuine.

187
00:10:01,400 --> 00:10:02,230
Hmm.

188
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:06,640
This crap is fake and you know it.

189
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:09,517
If this were actual papyrus,
it wouldn't rip so easily.

190
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:10,460
I'm no fool.

191
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:11,717
You should try a little.

192
00:10:11,800 --> 00:10:13,500
For the love of, where'd Mr.

193
00:10:13,620 --> 00:10:15,149
Joestar and the others go?

194
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:23,977
What's that Iggy?

195
00:10:24,060 --> 00:10:27,040
Why, you get back here, you little butt!

196
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:29,060
Hey, what about my body?

197
00:10:35,180 --> 00:10:36,280
Stupid dog.

198
00:10:36,580 --> 00:10:37,960
He managed to get away.

199
00:11:17,580 --> 00:11:22,497
Gotta say, if my hunch is correct, then
you've got a lot of balls, my friend.

200
00:11:22,580 --> 00:11:24,817
Seems like you're planning to attack me

201
00:11:24,900 --> 00:11:27,437
while we're in a crowd
of innocent bystanders.

202
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:29,560
Guys like you are a rare breed.

203
00:11:30,040 --> 00:11:34,805
Stand users don't usually show themselves,
let alone face their attacker head on.

204
00:11:35,880 --> 00:11:37,137
It's kind of noble.

205
00:11:37,220 --> 00:11:39,514
I didn't think you guys had that trait.

206
00:11:39,900 --> 00:11:40,980
Tell me your name.

207
00:11:46,460 --> 00:11:47,800
My name is Chaka,

208
00:11:48,100 --> 00:11:52,218
and my stand is known as Anubis, the
one true ruler of the underworld.

209
00:11:53,380 --> 00:11:55,440
Now then, Jean-Pierre Polnareff.

210
00:11:55,820 --> 00:11:57,996
Prepare to surrender your life to me.

211
00:11:59,500 --> 00:12:01,441
You want me to surrender my life?

212
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:04,795
Man, oh man, you sure don't
mince words, do you, Chaka?

213
00:12:04,880 --> 00:12:09,527
If nothing else, your confidence is more
impressive than your other companions.

214
00:12:17,300 --> 00:12:18,800
Give me your best shot.

215
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:22,609
Let's see if your Anubis stand
is all it's cracked up to be.

216
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:36,480
Come out, chariot!

217
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:43,300
He's brandishing his sword,

218
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:47,499
but is he really planning to fight
me with that instead of his stand?

219
00:12:52,660 --> 00:12:53,601
Something's off.

220
00:12:57,780 --> 00:13:02,800
His movements, his grip, his stance,
they're the dead giveaways of an amateur.

221
00:13:03,060 --> 00:13:04,707
But that doesn't make sense.

222
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:07,380
I need to keep my distance from him.

223
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:32,384
What the hell is going on here?

224
00:13:32,800 --> 00:13:35,077
His sword passed right through the pillar!

225
00:13:35,160 --> 00:13:40,101
And if that wasn't enough, he got me without
leaving even a single tear in my shirt!

226
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:43,729
If I hadn't stepped back when
I did, I would've been killed!

227
00:13:44,300 --> 00:13:46,240
You bastard! Chariot!

228
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:50,980
Damn it!

229
00:13:51,180 --> 00:13:55,415
Why don't you show yourself and face
me like a real fighter, you coward!

230
00:14:11,740 --> 00:14:12,570
Merd.

231
00:14:12,900 --> 00:14:14,520
This can't be happening.

232
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:15,880
I lost him.

233
00:14:16,240 --> 00:14:19,197
He could be hiding behind
any one of these pillars.

234
00:14:19,280 --> 00:14:23,221
Judging from his attacks, his sword
can pass through solid objects.

235
00:14:23,440 --> 00:14:27,877
And unfortunately for me, my chariot's
striking range is only about one meter.

236
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:28,790
Damn it.

237
00:14:28,873 --> 00:14:30,517
He's tougher than I thought he'd be.

238
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:33,097
I honestly can't believe
this asshole is actually

239
00:14:33,180 --> 00:14:35,817
giving me a run for my
money in a sword fight.

240
00:14:35,900 --> 00:14:39,720
But mark my words, you won't
have the upper hand for long.

241
00:14:42,240 --> 00:14:43,797
Hey Chaka, are you listening?

242
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:46,880
I've got a nice view, so
let's see what you've got!

243
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:50,197
There's no way you can sneak up
on me if I'm not behind a pillar!

244
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:53,339
Unless you're planning on
popping out of the ground!

245
00:15:05,900 --> 00:15:06,860
What the?!

246
00:15:07,840 --> 00:15:09,277
He's behind the pillar?!

247
00:15:09,360 --> 00:15:11,417
My sword doesn't need
to pass through objects!

248
00:15:11,500 --> 00:15:15,382
With the power of this blade, I
can cut through the pillar itself!

249
00:15:15,740 --> 00:15:17,580
Now die, Ponder F!

250
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:38,120
Man, that was a close one.

251
00:15:38,800 --> 00:15:42,565
That technique is so secret that
not even Jotaro knows about it.

252
00:15:42,840 --> 00:15:44,917
Silver Chariot can launch its rapier.

253
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:47,480
The downside is I only get one shot.

254
00:15:47,760 --> 00:15:49,720
My opponent dodges I'm history.

255
00:15:50,080 --> 00:15:53,080
A last resort once I've
exhausted my other options.

256
00:15:55,180 --> 00:15:57,220
While it's true I didn't kill you,

257
00:15:57,440 --> 00:16:00,911
I highly doubt you'll be getting
back up for another round.

258
00:16:01,260 --> 00:16:02,090
Huh?

259
00:16:05,520 --> 00:16:06,580
That's peculiar.

260
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:12,520
How the heck did it get
back into its scabbard?

261
00:16:12,740 --> 00:16:14,380
Did it slip in by chance?

262
00:16:28,780 --> 00:16:30,420
I didn't notice before,

263
00:16:30,860 --> 00:16:35,697
but now that I see it up close, I
fully appreciate the sword's beauty.

264
00:16:35,780 --> 00:16:38,120
I have to unsheathe it.

265
00:16:45,180 --> 00:16:46,520
Hey there, Polnareff.

266
00:16:46,680 --> 00:16:47,697
Thought we'd lost you.

267
00:16:47,780 --> 00:16:50,377
We were worried when you up
and vanished by yourself.

268
00:16:50,460 --> 00:16:53,048
We thought you'd been
ambushed by the enemy.

269
00:16:57,220 --> 00:16:58,380
Wait, are you okay?

270
00:16:59,220 --> 00:17:00,050
Huh?

271
00:17:00,133 --> 00:17:02,500
Oh, it's you, Mr. Joestar.

272
00:17:02,940 --> 00:17:04,957
I'm so fuzzy I can't think straight.

273
00:17:05,040 --> 00:17:07,117
Maybe it's from being tossed around.

274
00:17:07,200 --> 00:17:09,376
My injuries are worse than I thought.

275
00:17:13,440 --> 00:17:15,657
Polnareff, why are you
squatting like that?

276
00:17:15,740 --> 00:17:17,557
You didn't step and poop, did you?

277
00:17:17,640 --> 00:17:18,470
Huh?

278
00:17:18,960 --> 00:17:21,377
Polnareff, how did you
come across that sword?

279
00:17:21,460 --> 00:17:22,957
Did something happen out here?

280
00:17:23,040 --> 00:17:23,870
Yeah.

281
00:17:23,953 --> 00:17:26,837
I had a showdown with some
dirtbag that attacked me.

282
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:27,750
What?

283
00:17:27,833 --> 00:17:28,663
An enemy stand user?

284
00:17:28,746 --> 00:17:29,600
It's all over now.

285
00:17:30,020 --> 00:17:32,726
He said his stand was
known as the God Anubis.

286
00:17:33,720 --> 00:17:36,697
It was able to literally
phase through objects and

287
00:17:36,780 --> 00:17:39,537
cut them once it had a
target in its crosshairs.

288
00:17:39,620 --> 00:17:41,360
He was a strong foe.

289
00:17:41,520 --> 00:17:43,461
But despite his formidable power,

290
00:17:43,680 --> 00:17:45,097
when all was said and done,

291
00:17:45,180 --> 00:17:48,897
he was no match for the likes of
me, Polnareff reassured himself.

292
00:17:48,980 --> 00:17:51,197
He was using this sword as his weapon.

293
00:17:51,280 --> 00:17:53,160
Where did it go?

294
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:55,697
Where'd those rats come from?

295
00:17:55,780 --> 00:17:57,517
And why are they making off of the sword?

296
00:17:57,600 --> 00:17:58,541
Get out of here!

297
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:01,640
Jeez, talk about creepy.

298
00:18:02,160 --> 00:18:05,395
No one told me even the rats
steal stuff in this place.

299
00:18:06,520 --> 00:18:09,755
If you guys want to steal
something, steal some cheese.

300
00:18:13,020 --> 00:18:13,980
That's unusual.

301
00:18:14,700 --> 00:18:16,537
The sword's stuck in the scabbard.

302
00:18:16,620 --> 00:18:18,561
It's jammed in here really tight.

303
00:18:18,660 --> 00:18:20,040
Hey, Polnareff.

304
00:18:20,220 --> 00:18:22,177
While I'm relieved that you're all right,

305
00:18:22,260 --> 00:18:24,677
don't ever run off by
yourself again, got it?

306
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:25,642
It's dangerous.

307
00:18:25,820 --> 00:18:27,657
The enemy will find a way to attack you,

308
00:18:27,740 --> 00:18:30,328
even if you're just
alone for a few seconds.

309
00:18:32,500 --> 00:18:33,860
Oh crap, I forgot.

310
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:36,537
That's the sound of our
ship taking off without us.

311
00:18:36,620 --> 00:18:38,197
We need to hurry and get on board.

312
00:18:38,280 --> 00:18:39,657
We're heading to Edfa today.

313
00:18:39,740 --> 00:18:41,800
What? Come on, guys. Wait for me.

314
00:18:50,960 --> 00:18:53,977
Polnareff, so you decided to bring
the sword with you after all?

315
00:18:54,060 --> 00:18:56,297
Yeah, I'm going to turn
it in to the police.

316
00:18:56,380 --> 00:18:58,217
This thing is a dangerous
weapon, you know.

317
00:18:58,300 --> 00:19:00,100
Hmm, that's a good plan.

318
00:19:00,360 --> 00:19:03,777
Anyone could pick it up at those
ruins, so we can't take any chances.

319
00:19:03,860 --> 00:19:05,978
It's probably worth a small fortune.

320
00:19:11,940 --> 00:19:12,770
Quiet, Iggy.

321
00:19:12,920 --> 00:19:14,217
You can't make noise in here.

322
00:19:14,300 --> 00:19:16,829
If you keep this up,
we can get kicked out.

323
00:19:18,140 --> 00:19:20,677
What the hell is wrong
with that mutt today?

324
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:23,077
Ah, well, since the
damn dog won't shut up,

325
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:26,042
I guess I'll just take
the sword to the cops now.

326
00:19:26,180 --> 00:19:29,897
Polnareff, weren't you listening when
we told you not to go off on your own?

327
00:19:29,980 --> 00:19:32,333
Seriously, we talked about this earlier.

328
00:19:32,620 --> 00:19:35,497
Jotaro, tag along and keep
him out of trouble, would ya?

329
00:19:35,580 --> 00:19:36,410
Gotcha.

330
00:19:48,180 --> 00:19:51,651
Hey, shouldn't our first stop
have been the police station?

331
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:53,217
Oh, take it easy, Jotaro.

332
00:19:53,300 --> 00:19:56,712
A man's got to look his absolute
best, as the saying goes.

333
00:19:56,900 --> 00:19:58,200
Oh, before I forget.

334
00:19:59,260 --> 00:20:02,097
Old man, you mind putting this
over there out of the way?

335
00:20:02,180 --> 00:20:03,010
Sure.

336
00:20:03,093 --> 00:20:04,862
That thing's a dangerous weapon.

337
00:20:05,460 --> 00:20:07,757
All right, back to what
I was saying earlier.

338
00:20:07,840 --> 00:20:11,397
I did a fair amount of rolling around
and ended up getting kind of dirty.

339
00:20:11,480 --> 00:20:15,040
Make this face gorgeous
again, Mr. Barber. Will do.

340
00:20:17,260 --> 00:20:18,220
Ow! Ow!

341
00:20:18,700 --> 00:20:20,112
Hey, would you watch it?

342
00:20:20,240 --> 00:20:22,417
In case you haven't
noticed, that razor's dull.

343
00:20:22,500 --> 00:20:23,520
Come on, Mr.

344
00:20:23,660 --> 00:20:25,077
Barber, sharpen that thing.

345
00:20:25,160 --> 00:20:28,117
This is supposed to be the most
relaxing part of the haircut.

346
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:29,240
Oh, good grief.

347
00:20:29,620 --> 00:20:31,200
You're such a prima donna.

348
00:20:32,080 --> 00:20:33,280
You're right, sir.

349
00:20:33,660 --> 00:20:34,920
My apologies.

350
00:21:14,660 --> 00:21:16,760
Oh, better. Much better.

351
00:21:17,040 --> 00:21:18,393
Now that's a shave, Mr.

352
00:21:18,500 --> 00:21:19,330
Barber.

353
00:21:19,413 --> 00:21:20,537
That's what I'm talking about.

354
00:21:20,620 --> 00:21:21,460
Thank you.

355
00:21:22,500 --> 00:21:23,840
I'm glad to hear it.

356
00:21:24,320 --> 00:21:25,980
Tre Bone, barber.

357
00:21:26,300 --> 00:21:27,520
Tre Bone, man.

358
00:21:27,900 --> 00:21:31,320
And now, if you wouldn't mind
getting under my chin. Sure.

359
00:21:32,580 --> 00:21:33,620
Right here.

360
00:21:34,340 --> 00:21:36,860
Under your chin, yes. Hm?

361
00:21:37,520 --> 00:21:38,350
Huh?

362
00:21:41,100 --> 00:21:44,060
You did say under your
chin, right, Polnareff?

363
00:21:44,240 --> 00:21:45,380
What the hell?

364
00:21:46,800 --> 00:21:48,280
Remember me, you fool?

365
00:21:48,540 --> 00:21:51,658
I'm the Anubistan, and this
time you're going to die.

366
00:22:32,040 --> 00:22:32,940
Thank you.

367
00:23:25,800 --> 00:23:29,217
the sword is the stand
i won't lose twice to

368
00:23:29,300 --> 00:23:31,937
the same adversary this
guy's strong the more

369
00:23:32,020 --> 00:23:34,677
we fight this stand the faster it gets his

370
00:23:34,760 --> 00:23:38,360
eyes that stare this
time i'll take your head
